what what has been the most  rewarding thing for you for being santa  for this many years  well you know i've been very lucky to do  a lot of events with celebrities and  i've done tv and film and things like  that but  i think one of the important things is  to be grounded to be  you know know the base uh of what we do  with santa  and as i said earlier the number one  rule is the children  and volunteer work with the children i i  like i said at 4 500 santas and i  surveyed them and interviewed them and  uh  you know all of them do volunteer work  uh all over you know whether it's local  church work  school working fact a lot of times they  actually got started  because someone came to him saying would  you volunteer to do something for the  school  or the church or something like that so  the volunteer work is important  and i truly enjoy doing work with  children's hospitals in fact this year  i'll be doing a lot with hasselfeld  children's hospital in new york city  but i've done things with the ronald  mcdonald house and  i'm also the national santa for the  marine corps toys for tots  so i get to do a lot of volunteer work  uh we've done airlifts of toys  into uh areas that have been impacted by  hurricanes  natural disasters and so those are  the emotions you have with the families  and children  are very very special and when uh uh you  know children give me a hug all the time  you know  except this year of course but when it's  in it  when it's one of these special  situations where the family wasn't  expecting anything and you get that hug  and you see their face you know  i remember on dr phil we had a whole  bunch of children  after hurricane katrina and he brought  them all to hollywood and well actually  they were all in hollywood  uh living in southern california because  different churches had  brought them in and were helping them  while  uh their families were trying to get  resettled  and all of these families uh were  brought to  the paramount studios and they had a big  event and afterwards the children were  brought into an area where  they had filled the entire street with  toys  every type of toy you could think of and  dr phil  the the gates were closed and doctor  bill said okay we open the gates  it says you get one of every toy you see  and they open the gates of the kids ran  in  and i'm sitting there doing my homes and  having every time  but about 10 minutes in i'm standing  with some of the parents and the parents  are just  crying because they didn't expect  anything  they were wondering what they were going  to do for their children this year  and now their children had just  saw that santa opened his toy bag thank  you dr phil  and uh but again i'm sitting there  watering up when that happened so it's  it's those types of things i think that  give me a good base to work from  then i get to do the fancy stuff too you  know  would you say that's also the  characteristics of the  4 500 some santas that you've trained  that they have to have a heart for this  i think well again uh you have to be  real and we tell them that in the school  you know  you are santa and your job is to to  uh number one job is is the children and  you're there to serve the children  and to be santa to them and to answer  all their questions and  take care of all their uh and you can't  always give them the exact answer  they want but you have to listen to them  and you have to give them  uh hopefully some optimistic outlook  how do you do that in this season  it is hard you know the children are  wondering how we're going to get to the  house the parents are actually wondering  how do they  help their child get the letter to santa  so that santa can  uh you know respond to them um  the marine corps toys for tots during  spring months actually distributed like  three million  toys uh to children and families saw  around the country in areas that were  highly impacted and where the children  were  you know you're just you know it's  terrible you're stuck at home the  parents are stuck at home and  uh you know the parents don't have jobs  and it's just really rough  isn't it great to get the kids some  games or some books  keep their minds occupied and that's  something that  the marine corps did they have a little  side  thing that they do with the literacy uh  program  and so that's what they did they used  the books and the games for the kids  and this christmas uh we'll be doing  some airlifts i think we're gonna do one  in puerto rico and some other areas of  the country  unfortunately uh uh santa is a civilian  and so i can't go on some of these  military flights  to uh to be with the children and  families but the marines will get the  toys to them  and help them have a little better  [Music]  christmas

